{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1779478108,"nonce":"kL7rljvEETUBJdhm2TYlApgvCMc=","message":"Subagent/external-review synthesis for recurrence/state semantics, to guide the next schema/UX slice:\n\nDecision: do not refactor Feedbax into a full-State-only model where all leaf nodes become stateful wrappers. The current backend contract is the better long-term base: port wires are real per-step dataflow, and `StateIndex` is component-owned persistent state. Stateless leaves should keep threading state unchanged; stateful leaves/composites should declare owned state slots.\n\nThe missing primitive for this issue is first-class recurrence metadata. A direct self-loop such as `cell.hidden -\u003e cell.hidden` is valid, but only as a recurrent/cycle wire: source value at step N feeds target at step N+1. It is the same semantic category as the outer `network -\u003e mechanics -\u003e feedback -\u003e network` cycle, with a local hidden-state initializer. The schema/UI should distinguish:\n\n- instant wires: same-step dataflow, solid edge, must remain acyclic after recurrent cuts are removed;\n- recurrent wires: one-step delayed cycle edges, distinct visual treatment, typed init source, same shape/dtype checks as other wires;\n- state slots: owned `StateIndex` memory on a component, shown as component state/projection metadata rather than ordinary port wires.\n\nBackend implication: existing `Graph.step`/cycle support can remain the base, but Studio/schema should stop treating cycle classification as an invisible DFS side effect. Persist or derive-and-display `wire.kind = instant | recurrent`, require a recurrent initializer where runtime cannot derive one, and validate same-step cycles as errors.\n\nNetwork-specific implication: the opened Network subgraph must not hide GRU/LSTM recurrence. Either draw the internal hidden recurrent edge explicitly, or draw the hidden as an explicit state-slot projection with clear ownership/init. The current middle state, where the cell exposes hidden ports but the recurrence is omitted, is the confusing part.\n\nNested-cycle constraint: parent graph cycles plus subgraph-internal cycles are conceptually fine only if subgraph nodes are single-step components in the parent and recurrent cuts/init semantics compose. Until arbitrary nested cyclic graph lowering exists, keep `SimpleStagedNetwork` lowering as a bridge and do not imply that every nested cyclic Studio graph is executable.","files":null}]}